menu "Strip"

config APP_STRIP_MAX_PCT
    int "The strip's power ceiling, as a percent of full"
    range 0 100
    default 25
    help
        Eight WS2812B pixels at full white draw about 480 mA - 60 mA each, 20 mA a
        channel. On this board that was enough to brown it out: the strip lit at full
        white and the device rebooted under the audio load.

        The ceiling is the last stage of the frame, after the effect and the brightness,
        so no effect and no knob position can ask for more than this share of full
        power. It caps the current rather than the display: 25% is about 120 mA for
        eight pixels at white, and a single colour at the same 25% is a third of that.

        Raise it if the strip has its own supply with headroom; drop it if the board
        still resets. The measured figure is in docs/specs/led-strip.md, "Power".
endmenu
